<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Demo: Protected Area</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{prefix}}/user/o2p-base.css">
    {% if let Some(css_url) = custom_css_url %}
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{css_url}}">
    {% endif %}
    <style>
        .demo-description { color: var(--o2p-text-secondary); margin-bottom: var(--o2p-space-md); }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="container">
    <div class="page-header">
        <h1>Protected Area</h1>
        <nav>
            <a href="/">Home</a>
            <a href="/p1">p1</a>
            <a href="/p2">p2</a>
            <a href="/p3">p3</a>
            <a href="/p4">p4</a>
            <a href="/p5">p5</a>
            <a href="/p6">p6</a>
            <a href="/nested/p3">nested/p3</a>
            <a href="{{prefix}}/user/account">Account</a>
        </nav>
        <div class="header-buttons">
            <a href="{{prefix}}/user/logout?redirect=/" class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm">Logout</a>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <p class="demo-description">{{message}}</p>
        <p class="demo-description">
            This demo application showcases different route protection patterns.
            Each page below demonstrates a specific authentication and CSRF protection technique.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <div class="section-header">
            <h2 class="section-title">Demo Pages</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="item">
            <div class="item-detail"><a href="/p1">p1: AuthUser Extractor</a> — Route protection via extractor</div>
            <div class="item-detail"><a href="/p2">p2: Optional Auth</a> — Both authenticated and anonymous access</div>
            <div class="item-detail"><a href="/p3">p3: AJAX CSRF</a> — AJAX POST with CSRF token header</div>
            <div class="item-detail"><a href="/p4">p4: User Details</a> — User data via middleware Extension</div>
            <div class="item-detail"><a href="/p5">p5: CSRF in Template</a> — CSRF token embedded in template</div>
            <div class="item-detail"><a href="/p6">p6: Form CSRF</a> — Form submission with CSRF validation</div>
            <div class="item-detail"><a href="/nested/p3">nested/p3: AJAX CSRF</a> — Same as p3 under nested prefix</div>
            <div class="item-detail"><a href="{{prefix}}/user/account">Account</a> — Library-provided account management page (admin features shown for admin users)</div>
            <div class="item-detail"><a href="{{prefix}}/admin/index">Admin</a> — Library-provided user management (admin only)</div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
